Press patch 0004: make python-telegram-bot optional.
Purpose: python-telegram-bot 13.15 cannot be imported on Python 3.12 and later. Its vendored
urllib3 uses six.moves, and its fallback needs urllib3.contrib.appengine, which urllib3 2
removed. Press Settings imports the Telegram helper, so the whole Press Settings DocType failed
to load. With this patch Press imports without the package. Sending a Telegram message then
raises ImportError, which Press logs ("Telegram Bot Error") and marks the Telegram Message as
Error. Telegram alerts stay off in this image until Press moves to a maintained client.
Upstream: new proposal 5 in backend/docs/press-python314-upstream.md.
Remove when Press ships a Python 3.14 Telegram client (decision O-52 in backend/PROJECT-RECORD.md).

diff --git a/press/press/doctype/telegram_message/telegram_message.py b/press/press/doctype/telegram_message/telegram_message.py
index 3958261..b7fa996 100644
--- a/press/press/doctype/telegram_message/telegram_message.py
+++ b/press/press/doctype/telegram_message/telegram_message.py
@@ -7,7 +7,18 @@ import frappe
 from frappe.model.document import Document
 from frappe.query_builder import Interval
 from frappe.query_builder.functions import Now
-from telegram.error import NetworkError, RetryAfter
+
+try:
+	from telegram.error import NetworkError, RetryAfter
+except ImportError:
+	# python-telegram-bot 13.x cannot be imported on Python 3.12 and later (see telegram_utils).
+
+	class NetworkError(Exception):
+		pass
+
+	class RetryAfter(Exception):
+		pass
+
 
 from press.telegram_utils import Telegram
 
